Makes stdio's errors those of glibc and musl:
  - writing a stream opened only for reading, or reading one opened
    only for writing, fails with EBADF and sets the error indicator;
    mlibc took the bytes into its buffer and lost them when the flush
    failed (Lua's test suite checks this). Standard input is for
    reading and standard output and error for writing, as in glibc;
  - fwrite and fflush set errno when they fail, and fflush(NULL)
    returns EOF if any stream failed, instead of logging a warning to
    standard error and returning 0.
Meant for upstream.

